{"tag":"5V8I","kind":"remark","subkind":"hypothesis","paper":"2202.07745","version":"1","local":"ass-2","file":"","label":"ass:due","number":"2","section":"sec-2","order":2,"title":"Assumption","body_md":"\\label{ass:due}  {We suppose that there exists $N_0\\geq q$  such that, from}  $N_0$ onwards,\nthe rank of $f^N_{\\chi} $ is independent of $N$.   Such rank is denoted  by $q$.","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"ass","item":"context/hypothesis","head":"environment","counter":"ass","number_from":"counter","labels":["ass:due"],"scope":"paper","origin":"own","span":{"file":"Lippi-Deistler-Anderson-arXiv.tex","from":277,"to":279},"hash":"sha256:5039fa6d89da5f022142ac7e0d55aea49e1b8ce9254a5bd54d864116ae0d2895","minhash":"","census":"2202.07745v1#env-2","extractor":"ax/v0.5.19"}
{"tag":"N4U0","kind":"remark","subkind":"hypothesis","paper":"2202.07745","version":"1","local":"ass-3","file":"","label":"ass:tre","number":"3","section":"sec-2","order":3,"title":"Assumption","body_md":"\\label{ass:tre} The state dimension of a minimal, stable and miniphase state space realization corresponding to $f_{\\chi}^N$ is independent of $N$ {  from a certain $N_1$ onwards.}   Such state dimension is denoted by $n$.","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"ass","item":"context/hypothesis","head":"environment","counter":"ass","number_from":"counter","labels":["ass:tre"],"scope":"paper","origin":"own","span":{"file":"Lippi-Deistler-Anderson-arXiv.tex","from":286,"to":287},"hash":"sha256:adc913d52356aba2b72ba999172b873973c0afb81be2fa6e31f5b7ab4488f4a7","minhash":"","census":"2202.07745v1#env-3","extractor":"ax/v0.5.19"}
{"tag":"5Z91","kind":"remark","subkind":"hypothesis","paper":"2202.07745","version":"1","local":"ass-4","file":"","label":"ass:quattro","number":"4","section":"sec-2","order":4,"title":"Assumption","body_md":"\\label{ass:quattro} Weak cross-sectional dependence of $(\\xi^N_t)$. { The eigenvalues  $\\omega^N_{\\xi,1}(\\lambda)$ are uniformly bounded,} i.e. there exists $B\u003e0$ such that $\\omega^N_{\\xi,1}(\\lambda)\u003cB$  for all $N$ and $\\lambda$.","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"ass","item":"context/hypothesis","head":"environment","counter":"ass","number_from":"counter","labels":["ass:quattro"],"scope":"paper","origin":"own","span":{"file":"Lippi-Deistler-Anderson-arXiv.tex","from":297,"to":298},"hash":"sha256:bed5ec6654f4b6f8225319b98c8d2adb38d4f24fe8e6296cad3d00cdf525ceba","minhash":"","census":"2202.07745v1#env-4","extractor":"ax/v0.5.19"}
{"tag":"N6ZU","kind":"remark","subkind":"hypothesis","paper":"2202.07745","version":"1","local":"ass-5","file":"","label":"ass:cinque","number":"5","section":"sec-2","order":5,"title":"Assumption","body_md":"\\label{ass:cinque} Strong cross-sectional dependence of $(\\chi^N_t)$. The  eigenvalues $\\omega^N_{\\chi,s}(\\lambda)$, $s=1,\\ldots,q$, diverge as $N\\to \\infty$, $\\lambda$ almost everywhere in $[-\\pi,\\ \\pi]$.","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"ass","item":"context/hypothesis","head":"environment","counter":"ass","number_from":"counter","labels":["ass:cinque"],"scope":"paper","origin":"own","span":{"file":"Lippi-Deistler-Anderson-arXiv.tex","from":300,"to":301},"hash":"sha256:2a9168d85666e1c6dde8c5e03536a9720ea12bda473d37ac8e9cb81cad697adc","minhash":"","census":"2202.07745v1#env-5","extractor":"ax/v0.5.19"}
