{"tag":"1HC9","kind":"remark","subkind":"hypothesis","paper":"2202.07745","version":"1","local":"ass-7","file":"","label":"BBB","number":"7","section":"sec-4","order":7,"title":"Assumption","body_md":"\\label{BBB} For $q=r$, we assume that $k(0)=I_N$, i.e. $Q_0=I_N$ holds. For $q\u003cr$, we assume that the top $q\\times q$ submatrix of $k(0) $ is (1)~non-singular (which is the case generically) and  (2)~lower triangular (with non-zero diagonal elements).","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"ass","item":"context/hypothesis","head":"environment","counter":"ass","number_from":"counter","labels":["BBB"],"scope":"paper","origin":"own","span":{"file":"Lippi-Deistler-Anderson-arXiv.tex","from":502,"to":503},"hash":"sha256:e507123a1eee1e373742fb38a79d6ba661b5ac8bf0241c0f03237edc9fc48dd1","minhash":"","census":"2202.07745v1#env-7","extractor":"ax/v0.5.19"}
